    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d215">

                <pb facs="0567" n="545" xml:id="pg545"/>

                <head>No. 80.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to General Schenck</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-06-01"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 1,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The fifth Article of the Treaty requires the written arguments to be presented by
                    the 15th Jane.</p>
                <p>The adjournment of the Tribunal without amending that Article would, as we are
                    advised, practically amount to a discontinuance, and that Article can be amended
                    only by a new treaty.</p>
                <p>The opinion attributed to me regarding the Senate Article is very incorrectly
                    represented.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
